
 TLOAD puts a tape image from the MiSTer tape library on the tape drive,
 as if you had chosen it in the OSD. The library is the PDP2011 core's
 folder on the SD card (games/PDP2011) and the folders below it.

   TLOAD name              a .TAP or .TPC image, found in any folder
   TLOAD folder/name       ... from that folder (RSX/KIT.TAP)
   TLOAD                   what is on the drive
   TLOAD/UNLOAD            empty the drive

 Case does not matter. If two folders have a tape of that name, TLOAD
 lists them and you give the folder. TDIR lists the library. Mount the
 tape as usual after (MOU MS0:/FOR, MOU MS0:label, BRU, ...).

 The drive is MS0: (the core's Tape controller set to TS11) or MT0:
 (TM11). TLOAD will not change a tape that is mounted with a file
 structure or attached by a task, but it cannot see MOU/FOR or ALL: DMO
 or DEA the tape first.

 TLOAD needs the XE: driver and, on the MiSTer, MiSTer_pdp2011 with Host
 network not Off; elsewhere it says the library does not answer.
 HELP TLOAD EXAMPLE shows one.

2 EXAMPLE

   >TLOAD BB-J0830-01.L01_RSX11M+_V4.6_BRU_1999.TAP
   Loaded RSX/11M-PLUS_V4.6/BB-J0830-01.L01_RSX11M+_V4.6_BRU_1999.tap
   on MS0: (SIMH)
   >MOU MS0:/FOR
   >BRU /DIRECTORY MS0:
